Subject: [PATCH 15/31] Document Git-mode ignore handling

AGENTS.md, README.md and the website's getting-started page describe the
two modes (Git decides inside a Git work tree; the subset parser
outside), the git_unavailable refusal, the fingerprinted ignore sources
and the git_ignored restore guard. docs/AGENT-HOOKS.md notes git in the
hook environment and re-times the prompt hook (176 ms median in Git
mode). STATUS.md and CHANGELOG record the work, the dogfood and template
runs, and the open question about turns that edit .gitignore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
